  <title id="bdl16svgdparticles-title">SVGD particles on a mixture of three Gaussians after 1, 10 and 50 iterations</title>
  <desc id="bdl16svgdparticles-desc">Three square panels share the same target: an equal-weight mixture of three isotropic Gaussians drawn as concentric contour circles centered near (−2.5, 1), (2, 2.2) and (2, −2.2). One hundred particles start from a normal distribution with covariance 0.5 I at the origin. After 1 iteration they still form a single cloud near the origin. After 10 iterations most particles have reached the three modes but sit in tight clusters near their centers. After 50 iterations the kernel repulsion has spread them over the contours of each mode.</desc>
